+# User activity history — implemented, NOT deployed
+
+The current live release remains HfqeWOf_V3dYQaiV-LdjR. No activity tracking is live yet. Existing sync/account toggles are unchanged.
+
+Admin-only Settings → User activity shows successful sign-ins/sign-outs, completed visible page navigation, and recognized successful interactive actions (requests, reviews/ratings, watched state, lists, release follows, watchlists, issues, user settings). Filters: user, event kind, last 1/7/30 days, and authentication session; newest-first pagination, aggregate counts, links to opened pages and profiles. A session is an authentication session, not a measured visit duration. Existing logged-in users generate page activity without a fresh login.
+
+No historical backfill. Media links currently identify movie/series IDs rather than fetching extra titles. No query strings, search terms, review text, passwords, raw session IDs, IP addresses or raw user-agent strings retained. Session IDs are SHA-256 digests; only device/browser families remain. Client telemetry is session-only and server assigns actor/time. API-key jobs, GET polling, failed actions and hidden-tab navigation are excluded. Navigation is reported after completion with a short delay, duplicate suppression, no heartbeat and no awaited dependency for rendering.
+
+Storage: separate asynchronous SQLite/WAL user-activity.sqlite3 in the existing data directory, not the main catalogue database. Batches of 50, one-second flush, at most 1,000 queued events. Retain 30 days/100,000 events; prune on writes/reads and hourly while initialized. Failures do not fail user actions; dropped counts and last error are visible in the admin response, warnings throttled. This is best-effort usage history, not a durable security audit: a hard stop can lose the short pending batch, and dropped counters reset with process restart.
+
+Tests passed: policy/privacy, real SQLite restart persistence/retention/concurrent writes/pagination/100,000-event cap; actual Express route authorization, session spoof rejection, strict OpenAPI request schema; successful login/logout and mutations vs rejected/API-key/polling exclusions; actual client tracker visible/completed navigation, query stripping, duplicate suppression and cleanup; server rendering with mocked events/error state; bounded queue, failed storage and subsequent recovery. Server/client typechecks and targeted lint pass. Production build and live browser verification remain for a future deployment.
+
+Deploy manifest: tools/deployment/user-activity-release.json. New table is isolated and created lazily; no main database migration or toggle write. Rollback code disables collection while retaining the separate history file.
